From: Bartlomiej Dudzik <15948633+BobrImperator@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add `BehaviorItem::ready()`

Systems that must not override a queued transition guard on
`!behavior.has_transition()`. Add `ready()` as the named inverse so those
guards read as the condition they check. It is a provided method, so
existing `BehaviorItem` implementations are unaffected.
---
 src/lib.rs | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
index 0d29b1e..a1d6290 100644
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -193,6 +193,14 @@ pub trait BehaviorItem {
     ///
     /// Because of this, this method is useful to avoid unintentional transition overrides.
     fn has_transition(&self) -> bool;
+
+    /// Returns `true` if there is no pending [`Transition`] for this [`Behavior`].
+    ///
+    /// This is a convenience inverse of [`has_transition`](BehaviorItem::has_transition),
+    /// useful for guard clauses in systems that should skip entities with queued transitions.
+    fn ready(&self) -> bool {
+        !self.has_transition()
+    }
 }
 
 /// Query data for a [`Behavior`].
